# ============================================================================
# Merge strategy for the concurrent-session claim ledger (GG-082 / GG-101 / T-259)
#
# SESSION_CLAIMS.md is strictly APPEND-ONLY (one immutable row per session,
# keyed by UTC timestamp). `merge=union` makes two sessions' simultaneous claim
# appends auto-merge instead of colliding on push/rebase — both rows survive.
#
# NOTE: union merge is applied ONLY to this file precisely because it is the one
# governance file that is never edited in place. The other shared logs
# (DECISION_LOG.md, GOVERNANCE_GAP_LOG.md, TODO_NEXT.md, MEMORY_BANK.md) contain
# in-place edits (status flips OPEN->RESOLVED, "Last reviewed" header rewrites),
# where union merge would silently keep BOTH the stale and the new line. Those
# stay on the default merge driver and are protected instead by worktree
# isolation + path-scoped commits + the diff-against-HEAD rule (Hard Rule 10).
# ============================================================================
04_EXECUTION/SESSION_CLAIMS.md merge=union

# GG-103 (2026-07-15): .last_session_checkpoint reformatted from a single
# overwritten SHA to an append-only log (checkpoint<TAB>timestamp<TAB>slug
# rows), mirroring the SESSION_CLAIMS.md pattern above instead of inventing
# a new one. session-start reads only the LAST line; session-end APPENDS
# rather than overwrites. Same rationale as above: append-only + union merge
# means two sessions closing concurrently both survive instead of one
# clobbering the other's checkpoint pointer.
04_EXECUTION/.last_session_checkpoint merge=union

# ITERATION_MC_PROGRESS.md (2026-07-23): append-only completion log for the
# ITERATION_PLAN_MC_REMEDIATION_2026-07-22.md 4-window parallel workstream
# (A/B/C/D). Same rationale as SESSION_CLAIMS.md: multiple windows append
# "<TASK> DONE commit=<sha> — ..." lines concurrently; union merge means two
# windows finishing at the same time both survive instead of one clobbering
# the other's completion line.
04_EXECUTION/ITERATION_MC_PROGRESS.md merge=union

# OPERATOR_DIGEST_YYYYMMDD.md (2026-08-04, T-417): each session appends a new
# "## Update — later same day" section and never edits a prior one in place —
# genuinely append-only, unlike DECISION_LOG.md/TODO_NEXT.md above. Three
# concurrent same-day session-closes (T-413/VC6, T-415, T-414) each hit real
# conflicts on this file's default merge driver, forcing repeated manual
# resolution for content that was never actually in conflict. Union merge
# fixes that class of collision without the in-place-edit risk noted above.
11_MEMORY_HANDOFF/OPERATOR_DIGEST_*.md merge=union
